0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F4 16 Tf 108 624 Td (Let Us Keep Our Phones, But Not Use Them Everywhere) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 576 Td (I think the school has to be honest about one thing: a total ban will not work, and a total) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 552 Td (freedom does not work either. Last week I counted how often I picked up my phone during a) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 528 Td (Tuesday, and the number was forty-one. That is too many, and I want a rule that helps me) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 504 Td (bring it down. I also want a rule I can follow without feeling like I am being treated as a) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 480 Td (child.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 456 Td (My proposal has three parts. First, phones are off and in bags during lessons unless the) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 432 Td (teacher says otherwise. Second, phones are allowed at break and lunch in the yard and the) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 408 Td (library. Third, anyone who breaks the rule hands their phone to the teacher until the end of) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 384 Td (the lesson. It is clear, it is fair and a student can explain it to a parent in one) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 360 Td (sentence.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 336 Td (The reason I prefer this to a locker is trust. When a rule says we cannot be trusted at all,) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 312 Td (many students stop trying. When it says that lessons are for learning and breaks are for us,) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 288 Td (it gives us a reason to cooperate. I have seen this with the library rule, which most) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 264 Td (students follow without being watched.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 240 Td (A second reason is practicality. Lockers are far from some classrooms, and a queue at the) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 216 Td (lockers at the start of every lesson would waste time. Keeping the phone in a bag takes five) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 192 Td (seconds and nobody has to organise anything. Schools should choose rules that are easy to) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 168 Td (keep, because rules that are hard to keep end up being broken.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 144 Td (I realise that some people will still sneak a look under the desk. They will do that under) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 120 Td (any rule. What matters is that most students follow it most of the time, and that the ones) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 96 Td (who do not face a small and fair consequence. That is the kind of rule I would be happy to) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 72 Td (live with.) Tj ET
